<<<
duodecimo. See Fouio. Pl. -os; see -O(E)S 6.
===
**duodecimo.** See ^^FOLIO^^. Pl. *-os*; see ^^-O(E)S^^ 6.
>>>

<<<
duologue is a bad formation, but there are difficulties in the way of making a good one; dyologue, which is better only in one respect, is indistinguishable in sound from dialogue; dilogy conflicts with trilogy & tetralogy; dittologue suggests ditto; biloquy after soliloquy is less bad than duologue after monologue.
===
**duologue** is a bad formation, but there are difficulties in the way of making a good one; *dyologue*, which is better only in one respect, is indistinguishable in sound from *dialogue*; *dilogy* conflicts with *trilogy* & *tetralogy*; *dittologue* suggests *ditto*; *biloquy* after *soliloquy* is less bad than *duologue* after *monologue*.
>>>

<<<
The best course is to get along as well as may be with dialogue, duet, & periphrasis;
===
The best course is to get along as well as may be with *dialogue, duet,* & periphrasis;
>>>

